# deploy/embedder.env — the embedder's pins. KEY=VALUE lines only: no quotes,
# no export, no $ expansion, no continuation lines. Whatever fetches the model (the
# runbook's commands, or a host upgrade script that does the same, as root) reads this
# with a strict parser, so nothing in here may rely on a shell.
#
# Fetching the model: download
#   https://huggingface.co/<MODEL_REPO>/resolve/<MODEL_REV>/<MODEL_FILE>
# into the models directory (BRAIN_HOST_MODELS, /srv/brain/models by default), and
# start the embedder only once the file is exactly MODEL_BYTES long and its sha256 is
# MODEL_SHA256. The exact commands are in setup/runbooks/remote-brain.md, upgrade step 4.
#
# What is pinned and why: the image by the digest of its multi-arch index (it
# serves linux/amd64, linux/arm64 and linux/s390x, so one line is right for the
# Ampere VPS and for a dev box), and the model by repository revision AND content
# hash. A moved tag or a swapped file must fail loudly, not change what the
# vectors mean.
#
# deploy/compose.yaml repeats the image, the file name and the alias (compose
# interpolates only deploy/.env, and this file is for the host script). A test
# fails when the two disagree, so bump them together.
#
# Changing MODEL_ALIAS makes every stored vector stale, and the next
# `brain index --vectors` re-embeds all notes; set BRAIN_EMBEDDER_MODEL to the same
# name (it defaults to this one, and the engine looks up the model's query prefix by it).
# Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B (Apache-2.0) pools by the last token: compose passes `--pooling last`.
EMBED_IMAGE=ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp@sha256:b32890309c1a33a534a01b0b461e953dc2c5a6bac20213abcf48e22847a19c85
MODEL_REPO=Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B-GGUF
MODEL_REV=370f27d7550e0def9b39c1f16d3fbaa13aa67728
MODEL_FILE=Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B-Q8_0.gguf
MODEL_SHA256=06507c7b42688469c4e7298b0a1e16deff06caf291cf0a5b278c308249c3e439
MODEL_BYTES=639150592
MODEL_ALIAS=qwen3-embedding-0.6b
